---
// Public investor page: the idea, public market figures and why Dhaka. Numbers about our own business
// (unit economics, take rate, costs, milestones and their pass marks, the moat) are in the deck only.
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import F from "../data/facts.json";
import SceneHead from "../components/SceneHead.astro";
---
<Base title="Investors: amader.cloud" description="amader.cloud keeps idle devices working as a monthly service for families and companies, starting in Dhaka. Request the investor deck.">
<section class="page-head photo">
<SceneHead id="neighbourhood" />
  <div class="wrap">
    <h1>Reuse that pays every month.</h1>
    <p class="lede">Most devices people stop using still work. Today they're resold once, shredded, or left in a drawer. amader.cloud keeps them working: each idle device gets a new job or rents out the capacity it isn't using, run by us as a monthly service for families and companies. We're starting in Dhaka.</p>
    <div class="hero-actions" style="margin-bottom:0">
      <a class="btn btn-bulb" href="contact.html?topic=investor">Request the deck</a>
      <a class="btn btn-line" href={`mailto:${F.contact.invest}`}>{F.contact.invest}</a>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="wrap stack" style="padding-bottom:clamp(56px,8vw,112px)">
  <div>
    <h2>The market around us</h2>
    <ul class="ledger">
      <li><div class="fig">{F.stats.refurb.value}<small>{F.stats.refurb.label}</small></div><div><p>The global market for second-life devices. Almost all of it is one-off resale: the value ends at the sale.</p><cite>{F.stats.refurb.source}</cite></div></li>
      <li><div class="fig">{F.stats.itad.value}<small>{F.stats.itad.label}</small></div><div><p>What companies pay each year to retire their devices safely. In Bangladesh this market barely exists as a formal service.</p><cite>{F.stats.itad.source}</cite></div></li>
      <li><div class="fig">{F.stats.ewaste.value}<small>e‑waste, Bangladesh, {F.stats.ewaste.year}</small></div><div><p>Bangladesh, with {F.stats.population.bangladesh} people, produced this much e‑waste in a single year, and formally recycled very little of it.</p><cite>{F.stats.ewaste.source}; {F.stats.population.source}</cite></div></li>
    </ul>
  </div>

  <div class="split">
    <div>
      <h2>The idea</h2>
      <p>Reuse today ends at one transaction. Nobody keeps reused devices working <em>for</em> anyone. That's the business we're building: <strong>we operate reused devices as a service.</strong></p>
    </div>
    <div>
      <ul class="check-list">
        <li><strong>For people and for companies.</strong> Both have idle devices, and both get the same two outcomes: a new job, or income from spare capacity.</li>
        <li><strong>Monthly, not one-off.</strong> We look after every device we install, for as long as it works.</li>
        <li><strong>Safer than the drawer.</strong> Every device is wiped, kept updated and recycled properly at the end.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="panel-dusk">
    <h2>Why Dhaka first</h2>
    <div class="promises" style="border-color:#3d5186">
      <div><h3 style="color:var(--amber)">Dense and connected</h3><p>A city of apartment blocks and offices on fast local internet, so idle devices are close together and easy to link and look after.</p></div>
      <div><h3 style="color:var(--amber)">Subscriptions already work</h3><p>bKash and Nagad make small monthly payments normal, with no credit card needed.</p></div>
      <div><h3 style="color:var(--amber)">The rules just changed</h3><p>The Personal Data Protection Act 2026 makes keeping data local and wiping devices properly a legal question.</p></div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="panel-dusk cta">
    <div>
      <h2>The rest is in the deck</h2>
      <p style="margin:0;max-width:56ch">We're talking to angel and impact investors about funding the Dhaka pilot. The deck covers the business model, unit economics, milestones, team and the ask.</p>
    </div>
    <a class="btn btn-bulb" href="contact.html?topic=investor">Request the deck</a>
  </div>
</section>
</Base>
